<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!--
      Deliberately empty.

      This manifest used to declare android.permission.INTERNET, which the
      manifest merger then granted to every application embedding the binding.
      TalaDB is an embedded local database: it opens no socket, and the sync
      feature that once justified the permission was removed in 0.11.0.

      A library that silently adds INTERNET to its consumers is a problem for
      any app whose selling point is that it works offline — the permission is
      visible on the store listing and in the APK, and the app author cannot
      explain it. Consumers who do need it can declare it themselves.
    -->
</manifest>
